  {
   "id": "two-lines",
   "title": "Typical application: bidirectional protection of two lines",
   "page": 7,
   "description": "Each of two signal lines is tied to one cathode pin, and the common pin 3 goes to ground. A transient of either polarity on a line is clamped to ground through that line's diode pair, so the lines may carry signals swinging above and below ground.",
   "parts": [
    {
